    "raw": "First, we determine the cost of each of the first 3 pieces of art. Since John paid a total of $45,000 for these 3 pieces and they all cost the same, we divide $45,000 by 3:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Cost of each of the first 3 pieces} = \\frac{45,000}{3} = 15,000\n\\]\n\nNext, we calculate the cost of the fourth piece of art, which is 50% more expensive than the first 3 pieces. To find 50% of $15,000, we multiply $15,000 by 0.5:\n\n\\[\n\\text{50% of } 15,000 = 15,000 \\times 0.5 = 7,500\n\\]\n\nAdding this to the cost of one of the first 3 pieces gives us the cost of the fourth piece:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Cost of the fourth piece} = 15,000 + 7,500 = 22,500\n\\]\n\nNow, we sum the costs of all 4 pieces of art to find the total cost:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Total cost} = 15,000 + 15,000 + 15,000 + 22,500\n\\]\n\nWe can simplify this by first adding the costs of the first 3 pieces:\n\n\\[\n15,000 + 15,000 + 15,000 = 45,000\n\\]\n\nThen adding the cost of the fourth piece:\n\n\\[\n45,000 + 22,500 = 67,500\n\\]\n\nThus, the total cost of all the art is:\n\nFINAL: 67500",
